From: chrisohearn <137103567+chrisohearn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] PCI: apple: qualify the K114s for suspend-to-idle over
 the adopted N1 link

The adopted link's suspend check admits the J716c, the K114c and the
K116s. On a K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro, Mac17,13) with the
N1 described on port 0, every suspend-to-idle is therefore refused with
-EBUSY from the host's noirq suspend.

The K114s is the K116s's 14-inch twin: the same T6050 host, the N1 on
the port the boot loader trains, and in the macOS 27.2 (26B8125) Apple
device trees the two boards' PCIe nodes are identical. Unlike the K116s
tree it describes no second, kernel-trained port, so every device below
the host must still be in D0, as on the J716c and the K114c. Let it
through the same checks.

Compile-tested only (pcie-apple.o, clang 23, no warnings). Not yet run
through a suspend on a K114s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index 1b87ff0fa..0ac0675bb 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5774,9 +5774,15 @@ static int apple_pcie_check_adopted_s2idle(struct apple_pcie *pcie)
 	 * Qualified on the J716c, the K114c and the K116s. The K116s is the
 	 * J716c's OLED sibling: the same T6050 host, the N1 on port 0. Other
 	 * adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified.
+	 *
+	 * The K114s is admitted as the K116s's 14-inch twin: the same M5 Pro,
+	 * the same PCIe host and the N1 on the loader-trained port 0, and no
+	 * second port. It takes the K116s's checks; it has not been through a
+	 * suspend on the hardware yet.
 	 */
 	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c") ||
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c") ||
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114s") ||
 	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k116s")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
 		return -EBUSY;
 
